# std.prelude.testing: the prelude names of test code, the `std.testing`
# row of the spec's prelude table (spec/lang/10-modules.md#prelude,
# module.prelude.test-only). A module has them only in its test code: a
# `tests:` block, a test module, or an integration test module. The
# prototype joins this module, and so `std.testing`, only into a program
# with test code.
#
# `it` is compiler-provided.
pub use std.testing.{it}
